        "math_academy_id": "q-86181",
        "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x}{4}-\\frac{1}{4x}.$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x}{4}-\\frac{1}{4x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x)+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
